Hi Violet,
The empirical variograms themselves all look okay to me, though I can't see them contrasted to the fitted models. For amounts of data this small, you can also try CI="Gauss" and/or fast=FALSE in the variograms to improve their CIs and/or irregular time-lag dependence.
The tail end of the variograms don't really matter. There's only one data point (time lag) in that estimate.
You say that some home-range estimates come out very large. I can see that you've turned on the error model, but I can't see the fitted variograms. Did you check for outliers?
Best,
Chris

